# 8. Substitute the first, the Nth, or every match. Pement:
#   sed 's/foo/bar/'    sed 's/foo/bar/4'    sed 's/foo/bar/g'
# s/// changes only the first match on a line. A number as the flag picks
# that one match instead (here the 2nd "a"); g changes them all. Each line
# number address below sends one copy of the sentence to one form: watch
# which "a" turns into "u" on each line.
# Try: 3s/a/u/2g  changes the 2nd match and every one after it.
1s/a/u/
2s/a/u/2
3s/a/u/g

